n [Estimate, research brief].\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch classification: STALWART-to-FAST GROWER transition.\nCheckpoints: comps (10% Q2 [Actual]), store growth (115 openings FYE2027 [Actual]), inventory turnover (unsupported; [Unconfirmed]), and consistency of EPS growth (raised guidance twice in 2026 [Actual]).\n\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard:\n- Revenue growth (FY24-FY26 CAGR): (22.751/20.377)^(1/2)-1 = 5.6% [Arithmetic]\n- Operating margin (FYE2026): 11.9% [Tier 1]\n- EPS growth (FYE2026 vs FYE2025): 6.61 vs ~6.33? [Derived: 2.145/0.324416 = $6.61; prior ~?] [Estimate]\n- ROE: 38.98% [Aggregator]\n- FCF conversion: FYE2026 FCF 2.208 / NI 2.145 = 103% [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt/EBITDA: net cash $3.08B / EBITDA \u2248 2.65B \u2192 negative net leverage [Arithmetic]\n- Interest coverage: very strong (no interest expense in pack for FYE2026) [Tier 1 gap]\n\nJudgment: EXCELLENT.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (max 15):\n1. Buyback efficiency: 2/3 (buybacks at 30x+ earnings are value-destructive; but SBC dilution is low)\n2. M&A record: 2/3 (no major M&A; discipline)\n3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 (incremental ROIC well above WACC historically)\n4. Rationality of mix: 3/3 (reinvestment + buyback + dividend)\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3/3 (beat/raised Q1 and Q2 FYE2027 dramatically)\nInsider bonus: CEO ownership <5% (0); no insider net data [Unconfirmed].\nTotal: 13/15 \u2192 EXCELLENT.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550